SUMMARY:Earthquake: 2020 Aegean Sea earthquake (Turkey)
DESCRIPTION:An earthquake with a moment magnitude of 7.0 occurred on 30 Oct
 ober 2020 about 14 km (8.7 mi) northeast of the Greek island of Samos. Alt
 hough Samos was closest to the epicentre\, it was the large Turkish city 
 İzmir\, 70 km (43 mi) northeast that was heavily affected—more than 700
  residential and commercial structures were seriously damaged or destroyed
 .\n\nCrisis: Turkey\nSource: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Aegean_Sea
