SUMMARY:Earthquake: 2021 Haiti earthquake
DESCRIPTION:At 08:29:09 EDT on 14 August 2021\, a magnitude 7.2 earthquake 
 struck the Tiburon Peninsula of southern Haiti. It had a 10-kilometre-deep
  (6.2 mi) hypocenter near Petit-Trou-de-Nippes\, approximately 150 kilomet
 res (93 mi) west of the capital\, Port-au-Prince. Tsunami warnings were br
 iefly issued for the Haitian coast.\n\nCrisis: Haiti\nSource: https://en.w
 ikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Haiti_earthquake\nText: Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)\, 
